  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"The Visayas, an island group in the Philippines, plunged into crisis when the system operator, the Philippines grid operator, declared a red alert. This emergency response was triggered after Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2, a failing corporate asset, tripped offline—a critical equipment failure. Chronic system neglect from other long-running plant outages had already weakened the grid, while seasonal heat drove demand into a thin operating margin. The result was a massive power deficit: over 950 megawatts became unavailable, exposing the grid's vulnerability.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.85,\n      \"center\": \"who-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"focalized\",\n      \"focal\": \"who-0\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-0\", \"why-1\", \"why-2\", \"how-1\", \"result-0\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"Officials, acting as state enforcers, responded to the cascading power outage by imposing emergency load shedding. This crisis management action was a direct order to conduct load reduction on a critical 230-kilovolt transmission line to prevent overloading. The measure was necessitated by a vulnerable infrastructure failure—the tripping of a power plant component—and a severe energy demand spike. This control action, while stabilizing the grid, highlights a system forced to make harsh choices to manage a deepening power shortage.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.78,\n      \"center\": \"how-2\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-2\", \"why-0\", \"why-2\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"A technical malfunction at a power plant unit—the tripping offline of Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2—was the spark for a broader grid incident. This equipment failure, occurring amid extended outages from other plants, directly caused a supply shortfall that crippled the region. The system operator was then forced to activate crisis protocol, revealing how a single point of failure in critical energy infrastructure can trigger a widespread energy deficit across the grid.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.82,\n      \"center\": \"why-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-0\", \"why-1\", \"how-1\", \"result-0\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
